been leading you astray.

169
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:13,830
Attack!

170
00:10:13,980 --> 00:10:16,274
Hang her mouth open and hold her still!

171
00:10:16,620 --> 00:10:17,600
I'm not amused.

172
00:10:18,140 --> 00:10:20,669
I don't like it when
people think I'm weak.

173
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:32,880
Now you're all little black bears!

174
00:10:39,140 --> 00:10:40,280
The contract.

175
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:43,300
Oh no, she turned us into toys!

176
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:48,160
You shall follow my every
order until the day you perish.

177
00:10:49,460 --> 00:10:52,260
Don't tell me they
forgot about us already!

178
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:53,640
A bear army?

179
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:56,237
Where did all those
teddy soldiers come from?

180
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:58,977
And weren't we in the middle
of something just now?

181
00:10:59,060 --> 00:11:02,417
Kill everyone in the executive
tower and do it immediately!

182
00:11:02,500 --> 00:11:05,080
I can't disobey her orders!

183
00:11:05,480 --> 00:11:06,540
Kill everyone?

184
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:08,020
Including me?

185
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:15,220
Please, I don't want to do this!

186
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:17,675
Those bears must be working for Sugar.

187
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:20,297
I thought the only one she
had guarding her was Treble,

188
00:11:20,380 --> 00:11:21,897
but it looks like we were wrong.

189
00:11:21,980 --> 00:11:24,220
Leo, it's me, Flapper!

190
00:11:24,760 --> 00:11:26,820
All right, guys, get the enemy!

191
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:33,460
No! No! No! No!

192
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:39,077
Treble, come back at once!

193
00:11:39,160 --> 00:11:40,080
Give us a trap!

194
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:42,210
Treble!

195
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:44,350
Huh?

196
00:11:44,433 --> 00:11:45,263
A trap?

197
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:47,670
Hey!

198
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:49,977
Master Treble, please look!

199
00:11:50,060 --> 00:11:51,317
They're all starting to fight!

200
00:11:51,400 --> 00:11:52,820
It's utter chaos!

201
00:11:53,060 --> 00:11:53,897
You have to do something!

202
00:11:53,980 --> 00:11:54,810
Huh?

203
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:00,200
Hey, hey! You guys okay?

204
00:12:01,180 --> 00:12:02,800
I heard there's a dilemma.

205
00:12:03,460 --> 00:12:04,342
Master trouble!

206
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:06,580
Well, go on now.

207
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:08,537
Well, it's basically nothing, sir.

208
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:12,117
We're just a bit jumpy because
we found hornets in our cargo.

209
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:15,318
Rest assured, this won't
have any effect on our deal.

210
00:12:16,460 --> 00:12:17,920
She did lie.

211
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:24,100
Hey, hey, wait!

212
00:12:24,260 --> 00:12:25,420
Here comes trouble!

213
00:12:26,020 --> 00:12:28,120
Nice try! Hey, hey!

214
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:30,900
Who exactly are you, uh, a spy?

215
00:12:35,400 --> 00:12:38,860
Where did she go? Hey! Hey!

216
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:42,980
Wait a second, I know her!

217
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:47,597
She's in the strike!

218
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:50,400
That crew, how'd she get down here?

219
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:52,220
Dragon Ball!

220
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:54,720
Why are they going after Sugar?

221
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:55,980
Get back up here.

222
00:12:56,240 --> 00:12:58,597
You were fooled, you
good-for-nothing idiot.

223
00:12:58,680 --> 00:12:59,740
Die! Ah!

224
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:01,540
I'm mad now!

225
00:13:05,420 --> 00:13:07,240
Stinky, stinky, shay!

226
00:13:14,820 --> 00:13:16,360
Stick, stick him!

227
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:23,150
Meteora!

228
00:13:39,420 --> 00:13:40,297
I...

229
00:13:40,380 --> 00:13:42,820
I think Master Trouble is going crazy!

230
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:49,620
The executive tower, it's gonna wreck it!

231
00:14:18,420 --> 00:14:19,250
Usopp!

232
00:14:19,333 --> 00:14:20,200
Usopp, wake up!

233
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:28,100
I was worried. Robin! Shh!

234
00:14:29,980 --> 00:14:31,040
What happened?

235
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:33,720
Did we just get crushed by a big duck?

236
00:14:33,900 --> 00:14:35,959
The tentata have all been captured.

237
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:39,100
Drop dead, you crap head!

238
00:14:39,640 --> 00:14:42,052
Why don't you die first, you little brat?

239
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:45,760
Anyway, we're having a
serious conversation.

240
00:14:46,060 --> 00:14:49,220
So buzz off, you ready to talk yet?

241
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:51,420
I just said I'm not talking.

242
00:14:52,020 --> 00:14:52,980
Good boy.

243
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:54,740
Keep Usuland safe.

244
00:14:55,420 --> 00:14:57,538
Let's run while we still can, Robin.

245
00:14:58,420 --> 00:15:00,257
Truth is, he's a friend of mine.

246
00:15:00,340 --> 00:15:02,280
You can tell me. He is?

247
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:03,920
Oh, yeah.

248
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:05,637
His name is...

249
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:07,520
You mean Usuland? No!

250
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:10,437
You sure are dumb.

251
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:13,620
Um, you really think
he's my friend? Oh, no!

252
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:15,487
I fell right into your trap!

253
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:18,837
Are you friends with that
one-legged soldier, too? I...

254
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:20,160
I'm not telling.

255
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:22,000
Well, I already know.

256
00:15:22,220 --> 00:15:24,077
Oh, guess I can talk about it, then.

257
00:15:24,160 --> 00:15:25,500
Yeah, he's our friend.

258
00:15:26,060 --> 00:15:28,620
Actually, I didn't know. I'm a fool!

259
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:30,150
Interesting.

260
00:15:30,233 --> 00:15:32,520
I'm finally getting a clear picture now.

261
00:15:33,840 --> 00:15:36,380
Uh, it doesn't matter if you know or not.

262
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:38,481
You guys are finished either way!

263
00:15:39,700 --> 00:15:42,160
We're bringing them back no matter what!

264
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:51,000
Since we're sharing secrets
right now, I'll tell you it too.

265
00:16:01,820 --> 00:16:03,480
Is everyone okay?

266
00:16:18,420 --> 00:16:19,600
Yo, buddy.

267
00:16:22,540 --> 00:16:24,060
Gotta be more careful.

268
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:26,564
You should have made him angry.

269
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:28,780
You guys gave it your best shot.

270
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:31,380
But Treble is out of our league.

271
00:16:33,820 --> 00:16:35,760
I can still fight.

272
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:37,980
We won't give up.

273
00:16:40,820 --> 00:16:43,880
We'll finish Operation SOB.

274
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:49,580
Our friends are counting on us.

275
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:51,600
I believe in the commander.

276
00:16:52,060 --> 00:16:55,900
We have to help him defeat Doflamingo.

277
00:16:58,060 --> 00:17:00,480
We won't stop until he does.

278
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:05,717
He's waiting for us.

279
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:08,400
And we cannot let him down!

280
00:17:11,020 --> 00:17:13,060
There's no time to waste!

281
00:17:30,460 --> 00:17:31,940
Commander, no!

282
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:41,329
He's leaving the warlords?

283
00:17:41,540 --> 00:17:42,580
I don't get it.

284
00:17:42,780 --> 00:17:44,677
So he's stepping down
from the throne, too?

285
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:46,466
What's going to happen to us?

286
00:17:52,060 --> 00:17:53,320
He's nothing now.

287
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:54,598
A plain old pirate.

288
00:17:55,540 --> 00:17:58,364
The Navy won't let him
get away with his crimes.

289
00:17:58,480 --> 00:18:00,797
And this coliseum's going
to be the first thing to go.

290
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:03,056
Commander, did you see the newspaper?

291
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:04,897
Well, get our friends back.

292
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:06,797
And we don't even have to fight!

293
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:09,457
Just think of how many
lives will be saved by this!

294
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:11,260
We're lucky! No.

295
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:13,980
It was a false report.

296
00:18:16,320 --> 00:18:17,660
It was a lie?

297
00:18:21,260 --> 00:18:23,640
He's not leaving after all! All right!

298
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:25,557
Doflamenco's a great king!

299
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:28,097
There's no reason why he
should ever step down!

300
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:29,700
Our kingdom is saved!

301
00:18:29,980 --> 00:18:32,997
I'm going to enter today's competition
and win the Plain Plain Fruit!

302
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:36,080
And then, I'll be able
to defeat Doflamingo!

303
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:38,330
That's foolish!

304
00:18:38,413 --> 00:18:39,320
Have patience.

305
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:44,260
I know that you're angry,
and I feel the same way.

306
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:46,377
But the end is at hand.

307
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:48,166
My forces are ready to fight.

308
00:18:48,380 --> 00:18:50,060
I can handle this myself.

309
00:18:50,940 --> 00:18:52,660
I've waited! Long enough!

310
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:56,977
Our hopes have been dropped
from heaven to hell.

311
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:59,137
The fighters can't take this anymore!

312
00:18:59,220 --> 00:19:00,691
Their spirits are broken!

313
00:19:04,340 --> 00:19:08,060
All we can do now is
wait till the day we die.

314
00:19:10,920 --> 00:19:14,391
They say they'll release us if
we survive a thousand times.

315
00:19:14,540 --> 00:19:16,737
But how is that supposed to give us hope?

316
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:18,114
It's just more misery.

317
00:19:18,540 --> 00:19:21,960
The gladiator Kiros won
all 3 ,000 of his matches.

318
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:24,117
But that's just a stupid legend.

319
00:19:24,200 --> 00:19:25,729
No one even remembers him.

320
00:19:26,020 --> 00:19:28,237
Kiros was probably made
up by a bunch of prisoners

321
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:30,877
who were holding on to
a dream of being free.

322
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,417
But he's just a statue.

323
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:35,265
A perfect warrior who
could never really exist.

324
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:40,454
I'm sick of dreaming an
impossible dream, so I'll fight.

325
00:19:40,820 --> 00:19:44,997
The competition today is my
one chance, so I'm taking it!

326
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:46,433
It's a suicide mission!

327
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:49,461
We're not talking about a
typical gladiator match.

328
00:19:49,560 --> 00:19:50,720
You'll end up dead.

329
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,600
I forbid you to enter.

330
00:19:53,020 --> 00:19:54,820
You are not thinking straight.

331
00:19:55,100 --> 00:19:56,200
You are only 16.

332
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:58,737
Rebecca, I simply know better than you.

333
00:19:58,820 --> 00:19:59,650
Trust me.

334
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:01,660
You're not an adult yet.

335
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:04,259
You don't know what's good for you.

336
00:20:06,340 --> 00:20:07,500
Oh, shut up!

337
00:20:07,740 --> 00:20:09,740
Stop acting like you're my father!

338
00:20:10,620 --> 00:20:13,417
You are the one who's not
thinking straight here.

339
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:14,980
You can handle this!

340
00:20:15,260 --> 00:20:18,677
I don't know what your plan is,
but you can't beat the flamingo.

341
00:20:18,760 --> 00:20:19,760
Look at yourself!

342
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:22,200
You're just a broken toy with one leg!

343
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:27,600
Of course.

344
00:20:28,660 --> 00:20:29,600
You're right.

345
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:33,330
Wait!

346
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:40,280
I'm sorry for being so menacing,
but if you can, please do not fight.

347
00:20:40,840 --> 00:20:41,670
Seltzer!

348
00:20:41,840 --> 00:20:43,020
We can talk!

349
00:20:43,260 --> 00:20:44,300
Just come back!

350
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:45,900
Seltzer, please!

351
00:20:46,340 --> 00:20:47,940
Don't leave like this!

352
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:49,200
I'm scared!

353
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:52,226
I didn't want you to
sacrifice yourself, okay?

354
00:20:52,320 --> 00:20:53,150
That's all!

355
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:54,360
I'm sorry!

356
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:56,960
I'm just so worried about you!

357
00:20:57,660 --> 00:20:59,240
Please, come back!

358
00:21:19,740 --> 00:21:23,300
This is the first time I've
ever seen Rebecca attack!

359
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:25,346
She's going on the offensive!

360
00:21:25,960 --> 00:21:28,540
Hold on, what's with that sword?

361
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:31,180
The blade isn't even sharp, is it?

362
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:35,737
In this coliseum we fight
to the death if you won't

363
00:21:35,820 --> 00:21:38,697
shed the blood of others
You'll pay with your own.

364
00:21:38,780 --> 00:21:42,500
That's what the audience
wants to see after all now

365
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:03,030
Damn!

366
00:22:04,020 --> 00:22:05,380
Hey! Muscle melon!

367
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:07,500
Are you talking to me?

368
00:22:08,120 --> 00:22:09,591
Protect her for me, okay?

369
00:22:10,520 --> 00:22:11,350
Whaaaaat?

370
00:22:11,433 --> 00:22:13,960
Say, Rebecca, here's a question.

371
00:22:14,320 --> 00:22:17,614
Do you happen to know how
your dear Mother Scarlet died?

372
00:22:20,460 --> 00:22:22,754
I'm going to bring us something to eat.

373
00:22:25,540 --> 00:22:27,940
I saw the toy soldier that day.

374
00:22:28,820 --> 00:22:31,060
He cried like a baby. Pathetic.

375
00:22:34,420 --> 00:22:35,377
I'm sorry.

376
00:22:35,460 --> 00:22:36,637
It's my fault.

377
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:38,820
I failed to protect your mother.

378
00:22:46,880 --> 00:22:48,640
That's not just my legs.

379
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:51,620
Pika must be moving.

380
00:22:51,900 --> 00:22:54,606
I wonder if he's dealing
with someone as well.

381
00:22:57,800 --> 00:22:59,140
Stay right there.

382
00:22:59,860 --> 00:23:01,566
Are you all right, Commander?

383
00:23:02,200 --> 00:23:03,340
Yes, thank you.

384
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:05,280
We've got to move! Hold on.

385
00:23:05,500 --> 00:23:07,097
They'll be hurt if we don't help them.

386
00:23:07,180 --> 00:23:09,800
Get your paws off me,
young little bastards!

387
00:23:10,180 --> 00:23:12,540
Stop looking back, Commander. Just go!

388
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:14,930
We're ready.

389
00:23:15,140 --> 00:23:17,140
We all knew what we signed up for.

390
00:23:17,320 --> 00:23:18,202
Don't say that.

391
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:20,960
If you stay here, then everyone might die.

392
00:23:22,320 --> 00:23:26,260
Even if Leo pulls off Operation
SOP, it's still not over.

393
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:30,617
If we let Doflamingo walk away, he
can do the same thing all over again.

394
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:31,620
Or even worse!

395
00:23:31,800 --> 00:23:33,637
No one else can beat Toe Flamingo.

396
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:35,544
We're counting on you for that.

397
00:23:35,720 --> 00:23:36,550
Keep fighting!

398
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:39,477
Is the commander really
such a big deal, Leo?

399
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:40,390
I don't know.

400
00:23:40,560 --> 00:23:43,442
Seems kind of crazy to
bet everything on one guy.

401
00:23:44,160 --> 00:23:45,637
Why do you trust him so much?

402
00:23:45,720 --> 00:23:47,308
He's just a one-legged toy!

403
00:23:48,280 --> 00:23:50,986
Normally, when Sugar
turns someone into a toy,

404
00:23:51,160 --> 00:23:53,477
they're bound by the contract she makes.

405
00:23:53,560 --> 00:23:55,148
meaning they can't disobey.

406
00:23:55,660 --> 00:23:58,057
That's why they're able to
keep them all as slaves.

407
00:23:58,140 --> 00:24:00,640
But unlike them, the commander's free.

408
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:03,528
He was the first one
here to be transformed.

409
00:24:03,680 --> 00:24:06,657
So that time when Sugar
used her hobby-hobby power,

410
00:24:06,740 --> 00:24:11,700
she made a mistake and forgot
to form a contract with him.

411
00:24:13,200 --> 00:24:15,897
One little error from
more than ten years ago

412
00:24:15,980 --> 00:24:18,509
gave them a powerful
enemy like none other.

413
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:23,386
He's the only toy in this kingdom who can
strike back at the Don Quixote family.

414
00:24:23,600 --> 00:24:25,980
A toy who can take revenge for them all.

415
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:30,200
For a whole decade,

416
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:34,852
he's been fighting on his own, but he
never gave up and he never lost hope.

417
00:24:37,080 --> 00:24:40,997
He knew the truth about the toys
and how much they were suffering,

418
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:43,180
slaving away and forgotten.

419
00:24:44,940 --> 00:24:48,720
In time, all our people would
have been enslaved as well,

420
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:54,820
but thanks to him, now
we're able to fight back.

421
00:24:59,700 --> 00:25:02,440
If he calls us to arms, we have to answer!

422
00:25:03,420 --> 00:25:06,020
Otherwise, this kingdom
is as good as dead!

423
00:25:10,760 --> 00:25:11,860
He's worth it!

424
00:25:12,060 --> 00:25:14,825
We're proud to bet
everything we've got on him!

425
00:25:18,260 --> 00:25:23,860
Nobody remembers him now, but years ago,
everyone in the kingdom knew who he was.

426
00:25:25,480 --> 00:25:30,680
Before he got transformed into
a toy, his name was Kiros.

427
00:25:31,920 --> 00:25:36,180
He was the strongest gladiator
that the Colosseum had ever seen.

428
00:25:38,080 --> 00:25:39,857
That's who our commander is.

429
00:25:39,940 --> 00:25:41,760
A legendary hero.
